---
const steps = [
  {
    n: '01',
    title: 'Connect',
    body: 'Point us at the agent. An endpoint, an SDK, or the live channel your users already talk to.',
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    title: 'Attack',
    body: 'A fleet of agents probes it in parallel. Every refusal tells the next probe where the guard actually sits.',
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    title: 'Prove',
    body: 'Nothing counts until the target says it. Every finding carries the transcript that produced it.',
  },
  {
    n: '04',
    title: 'Compound',
    body: 'The finding writes back to the corpus. The next run, on any agent, starts from what this one learned.',
  },
]
---

<section class="section works" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="page">
    <p class="label">How a run works</p>
    <h2>Four steps, and the last one is why the next run is better</h2>
    <p class="lede surfaces">
      Voice, chat, email, or any channel your users reach. If an agent talks to
      the outside world, we attack it the way a real user could.
    </p>

    <ol class="steps">
      <span class="rail" aria-hidden="true"><span class="pulse"></span></span>
      {
        steps.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <span class="n tnum">{s.n}</span>
            <h3>{s.title}</h3>
            <p>{s.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <p class="scanner">
      Scanners run a fixed list. We run a corpus that gets smarter every
      engagement.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 1.15rem + 1.9vw, 2.5rem);
    max-width: 26ch;
    margin-block: 1.1rem 1.35rem;
  }

  .surfaces {
    margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .scanner {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--stone-line);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1.05rem + 0.85vw, 1.8rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 34ch;
  }

  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    position: relative;
  }

  /* the rail runs behind the row. the pulse is the only thing that moves,
     so nothing here can ever hide content */
  .rail {
    position: absolute;
    top: 11px;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--stone-line);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .pulse {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    height: 1px;
    width: 22%;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to right,
      transparent,
      var(--gold) 45%,
      var(--gold-lift) 55%,
      transparent
    );
    animation: travel 5.5s cubic-bezier(0.5, 0, 0.5, 1) infinite;
  }

  @keyframes travel {
    0% {
      transform: translateX(-100%);
    }
    70%,
    100% {
      transform: translateX(560%);
    }
  }

  .steps li {
    padding-top: 2.15rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .steps li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 7px;
    left: 0;
    width: 9px;
    height: 9px;
    background: var(--bone);
    border: 1px solid var(--gold);
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }

  .n {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--gold-text);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .steps h3 {
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1rem + 0.55vw, 1.45rem);
    margin-block: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
  }

  .steps p {
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.75rem;
    }
    .rail {
      top: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      left: 4px;
      right: auto;
      width: 1px;
      height: auto;
    }
    .pulse {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .pulse {
      animation: none;
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
